 read it word by word so get this  it starts off by saying throughout his  time in the spider-man suit tom holland  has got to shoot some spectacular stuff  rubbing shoulders with the avengers in  captain america civil wars epic airport  fight spending plenty of time with tony  stark and spider-man homecoming and  playing a significant part in the fight  back against thanos in avengers infinity  war and in-game but  in the upcoming spider-man no way home  the actor tells empire that he filmed  one of the coolest scenes i've ever shot  a sequence including a character he  wasn't at liberty to divulge so right  off the bat when you hear  tom holland can't mention who a  character is in a scene you  automatically think well this has got to  be toby mcguire's character or andrew  garfield's character but they actually  give us more to believe that this is  indeed the case it goes on to say what  he could say is that the scene features  his peter parker and i stress that it  literally says his peter parker marissa  tomei's aunt may and john favreau's  happy hogan along with a mystery fourth  character now it gets even better but  let me just stress how they are having  to specify  which characters these are they  literally say his peter parker and they  have to clarify it's marissa tomei's  aunt may and it's john f rose happy  hogan now i didn't think that there  would be another happy hogan in the film  there might not be but i think there  might be more than one aunt may in the  film which is why they have to specify  here and i think we all know why they  have to specify which peter parker this  is here's what tom holland had to say  about the scene it's four people sitting  at a table having a conversation about  what it's like to be a superhero and it  was amazing the other day we watched the  scene my brother and i and our jaws were  on the floor okay can we really expect  him to be talking about anyone besides  toby or andrew maybe matt murdock but  i'll touch on 